IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `iposa-offences`

-- Intellectual Property Office of Singapore Act 2001, ss 2, 11, 29, 30, 31, 33, 36 and Third Schedule -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_intellectual-property-office-of-singapore-act-2001.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a card-carrying officer asking a suspect seller for ID` MEANS Demand WITH
    `the officer declared the office and produced the card` IS TRUE
    `the offence is covered` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believes the person committed it` IS TRUE
    `the order is in writing` IS FALSE
    `the person is within Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the person appears acquainted with the circumstances` IS FALSE

`an officer who did not show a card` MEANS Demand WITH
    `the officer declared the office and produced the card` IS FALSE
    `the offence is covered` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believes the person committed it` IS TRUE
    `the order is in writing` IS FALSE
    `the person is within Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the person appears acquainted with the circumstances` IS FALSE

`a written summons to a witness in Singapore` MEANS Demand WITH
    `the officer declared the office and produced the card` IS TRUE
    `the offence is covered` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believes the person committed it` IS FALSE
    `the order is in writing` IS TRUE
    `the person is within Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the person appears acquainted with the circumstances` IS TRUE

`an oral summons to a witness` MEANS Demand WITH
    `the officer declared the office and produced the card` IS TRUE
    `the offence is covered` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believes the person committed it` IS FALSE
    `the order is in writing` IS FALSE
    `the person is within Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the person appears acquainted with the circumstances` IS TRUE

`a shopkeeper who blocks the door` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `obstructed or refused access` IS TRUE
    `wilfully mis-stated` IS FALSE
    `mis-stated by honest mistake` IS FALSE
    `refused information or documents` IS FALSE
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing` IS FALSE
    `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS FALSE

`a trader who lies about invoices` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `obstructed or refused access` IS FALSE
    `wilfully mis-stated` IS TRUE
    `mis-stated by honest mistake` IS FALSE
    `refused information or documents` IS FALSE
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing` IS FALSE
    `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS FALSE

`a clerk who misremembers a date` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `obstructed or refused access` IS FALSE
    `wilfully mis-stated` IS FALSE
    `mis-stated by honest mistake` IS TRUE
    `refused information or documents` IS FALSE
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing` IS FALSE
    `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS FALSE

`a refusal with a lawful excuse` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `obstructed or refused access` IS FALSE
    `wilfully mis-stated` IS FALSE
    `mis-stated by honest mistake` IS FALSE
    `refused information or documents` IS TRUE
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing` IS TRUE
    `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS FALSE

`a refusal without excuse` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `obstructed or refused access` IS FALSE
    `wilfully mis-stated` IS FALSE
    `mis-stated by honest mistake` IS FALSE
    `refused information or documents` IS TRUE
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing` IS FALSE
    `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS FALSE

